{
  "_source": "Ministry of Education, Science, Vocational Training and Early Education / Curriculum Development Centre, Zambia. 'Commerce and Principles of Accounts Syllabus, Grades 10-12' (2013, ISBN 9982-00-567-7) -- Commerce, Grade 12, Topics 12.1-12.6. Topic, sub-topic and Specific Outcome statements only (Knowledge/Skills/Values omitted, as elsewhere in this app). TERM PLACEMENT IS NOW FULLY REAL: a complete real 'Grade 12 Commerce Scheme of Work, Term 1-3' (a real Zambian secondary school; the source's own teacher name, school name, Teaching Service number and phone number are not reproduced here per this app's standing sourcing policy) was shared with this project and reviewed in full, superseding an earlier partial (Term-1-only) version of this same scheme. It confirms: Term 1 covers all of 12.1 Insurance plus the Postal Services sub-topic (12.2.1) of Communication; Term 2 covers the Telecommunication Services sub-topic (12.2.2) of Communication, all of 12.3 Transport, and the 'types' half of Warehousing (renamed 12.4.1 Types of Warehouses, its own single competency); Term 3 covers the 'functions' half of Warehousing (split out into its own new sub-topic, 12.4.2 Functions of Warehouses, carrying the competency this file previously grouped together with 12.4.1), plus all of 12.5 Advertising and 12.6 Production and Commerce versus Environment. This replaces the file's earlier non-sourced organizational split (which had grouped all of 12.2-12.6 into Term 2/3 evenly). The only structural change beyond term placement is this one sub-topic split -- 12.4's two competencies, previously combined under a single 12.4.1 Types of Warehouses sub-topic, are now two sub-topics (12.4.1 Types, 12.4.2 Functions) matching how the real scheme of work actually teaches them a term apart; no competency wording, topic, or objective was added, removed, or altered.",
